<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Ava Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1364 CE – 1555 CE · capital Ava</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The dominant kingdom of Upper Burma for nearly two centuries, which fought the Mon of Hanthawaddy for forty years and shaped classical Burmese literature.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After Shan raiders sacked <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pinya-kingdom">Pinya</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sagaing-kingdom">Sagaing</a> in 1364, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thado-minbya">Thado Minbya</a> united the two courts and in 1365 founded a new capital at Ava, Inwa, at the confluence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irrawaddy-river">Irrawaddy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/myitnge-river">Myitnge</a> rivers. He presented his kingdom as the successor of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/pagan-kingdom">Pagan Kingdom</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Ava controlled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyaukse">Kyaukse</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minbu">Minbu</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> lands and claimed authority over <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prome-kingdom">Prome</a>, Toungoo and the Shan borders. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swa-saw-ke">Swa Saw Ke</a> and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minkhaung-i">Minkhaung I</a> fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/forty-years-war">Forty Years' War</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/razadarit">Razadarit</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hanthawaddy-kingdom">Hanthawaddy Kingdom</a> from 1385 to 1424. Monks and court poets such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shin-maha-thilawuntha">Shin Maha Thilawuntha</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shin-maha-rahtathara">Shin Maha Rahtathara</a> made Ava the golden age of Burmese classical literature.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Ava weakened as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> broke away, including <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prome-kingdom">Prome</a> and Toungoo. In 1527 a confederation of Shan states led by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mohnyin">Mohnyin</a> captured Ava, ruling it as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/confederation-of-shan-states">Confederation of Shan States</a>. In 1555 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayinnaung">Bayinnaung</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-toungoo-empire">First Toungoo Empire</a> conquered it, and Ava later became the capital of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/restored-toungoo-kingdom">Restored Toungoo Kingdom</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ava-kingdom.jpg" alt="Ava Kingdom" width="320" height="634"><figcaption>Image: Hybernator · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Burma_in_1450.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1364 CE – 1555 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ava</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Thado Minbya, Minkhaung I, Mohnyin Thado</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Burmese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/myanmar">Myanmar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Ava, Inwa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1460&amp;focus=ava-kingdom" aria-label="Ava Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7254 1370 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ava Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7574 1626L7575 1626M7574 1626L7574 1625M7574 1626L7609 1732M7574 1626L7577 1736M7574 1626L7511 1673"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7575 1626h0M7574 1625h0M7609 1732h0M7577 1736h0M7511 1673h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7574 1626h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7574 1626h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1460&amp;focus=ava-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
